drg: flush a page above 4 GB by its real address (patch 0912)

pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys() shifted the 32-bit page number before
widening it: (vm_offset_t)(pp << PAGE_SHIFT). This phone's XNU RAM runs to
0x17e4c0000, so a page above 4 GB lost its top bits. Boot #37 panicked in
it: DrgGPU mapped a GPU object write-combined (pmap_set_cache_attributes ->
this flush) on page 0x5ed92 (0x17b648000), and phystokv_range got
0x7b648000 ("illegal PA ... phys base 0xae000000"). Widen first, as every
other page shift in the arm pmap does (ptoa, pmap_enter_addr).

diff --git a/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c b/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
index 00568d3..8cdc914 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
@@ -6881,7 +6881,7 @@ void
 pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys(
 	ppnum_t pp)
 {
-	flush_dcache((vm_offset_t) (pp << PAGE_SHIFT), PAGE_SIZE, TRUE);
+	flush_dcache(((vm_offset_t) pp) << PAGE_SHIFT, PAGE_SIZE, TRUE);
 }
 
 #if CONFIG_COREDUMP
